1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:08,220
On Slide 35, we define our 3-Tier Governance Spectrum for balancing autonomy and control.

2
00:00:08,920 --> 00:00:15,140
This is the golden rule of agent architecture. Not all tasks carry the same risk!

3
00:00:15,840 --> 00:00:30,980
Tier 1 is Full Autonomy. These are low-risk, read-only tasks—like scanning RSS feeds, organizing folder tags, or reading research papers. Let your avatar run freely!

4
00:00:31,680 --> 00:00:44,620
Tier 2 is Notify & Log. Medium-risk tasks—like drafting customer emails or generating code branches. The avatar performs the work and logs it, notifying you of the outcome.

5
00:00:45,320 --> 00:01:02,580
Tier 3 is Strict Human Approval. High-risk write operations—like sending emails to clients, executing live database migrations, or spending money. The avatar prepares everything, but waits for your explicit click to send!

6
00:01:03,280 --> 00:01:08,870
This 3-tier matrix eliminates risk while preserving 90% of the speed benefits.

